1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,650
Adding a reranker is supposed to
make search better.

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:06,525
On legal text, it made it worse.

3
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:13,093
In the LegalBench-RAG experiments, the authors
added a general-purpose reranker to

4
00:00:13,093 --> 00:00:14,175
legal retrieval.

5
00:00:14,783 --> 00:00:17,658
It performed worse than no
reranker at all.

6
00:00:17,958 --> 00:00:20,408
They put it down to domain mismatch.

7
00:00:20,708 --> 00:00:23,908
General-purpose doesn't mean it
fits your domain.

8
00:00:24,917 --> 00:00:30,420
So evaluate any off-the-shelf reranker on your
own legal queries before you adopt

9
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:33,817
it, and keep it only if
span-level recall goes up.

10
00:00:34,817 --> 00:00:37,442
The full article is on vidyal.ai.
